790	// TestResolveCLIEncodedBasePathJoin drives the encoded-base-path join the way
791	// a user does: the upstream carries a percent-encoded userinfo, an IPv6 host
792	// with brackets, a port and a base path with encoded slashes and trailing
793	// slash runs. Only the junction run collapses to one slash; every other byte
794	// of the configured upstream and the request target must reach upstreamURL
795	// unchanged. The routes define no queryTransforms, so the raw query (empty
796	// question mark included) is preserved verbatim. Everything runs offline:
797	// the upstream hosts never need to exist.
